    "summary": "Added src/daemon/__tests__/git-hooks-real-git.test.ts: a temporary remote and two clones, hooks installed through repo.gitHooks.install; a real merging git pull runs post-merge and a real git pull --rebase runs post-rewrite (the recording stand-in entry gets the repository root and hook name and exits 1), git exits 0 each time, and with the entry file deleted a pull --rebase still exits 0 and status still shows both blocks. Documented the feature and its limits (terminal push gap, hook managers, foreign early exit, worktrees, moved daemon, explicit refresh) in docs/plans/team-workflow.md. The sweep ran by area against a clean base worktree (52c23f143) and is recorded in S001/SWEEP.md: identical failures except repo-call-audit and repo-call-table, which fail only on the other session's design-review-step.recover/failure phases; the gitHooks methods they first reported were fixed by listing them in handler-runtime.ts text.",
